{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>עדת</b> — It departed and passed from you. I have no knowledge to know what these seven עדנין are — whether days or weeks or months or years. That they are days or weeks is not sound, because it is written: \"until his hair grew like eagles' [feathers].\" The Gaon [Saadia] said: they are months. In my opinion they are years, as in: עדן and עדנין and פלג עדן. Do not entertain the notion that Nebuchadnezzar became an actual beast, male or female, for it is written only that he would dwell with the beasts and eat grass like them. The meaning of ולבב חיוא is that his mind departed — and that is the mind of the soul — and when the wisdom of the soul departs, his heart returns and he remains like the heart of a beast. The proof for all this is what he says at the end: \"my eyes were lifted to heaven and my knowledge returned to me.\" I myself saw one of our companions, trustworthy in spirit, who told me that he was on a certain island called Sardania, and a certain uncircumcised man had gone out and fled from his family, for his mind had departed and he went mad, and he was among the deer for many years, walking on his hands and feet like them. The king of the island went out to hunt and captured many deer, and that foolish uncircumcised man of importance was caught as a deer. His family came and recognized him and spoke to him, but he did not answer. They set bread before him to eat and wine to drink, but he refused. They gave him grasses with the deer and he ate, and at midnight he fled to the deer of the field."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:59.499236176Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}